"Mission Oflameron" Screenplay

The action takes place in the distant future. The Central Command (most likely a highly developed Artificial Intelligence) receives data about the existence of a Virtual Consciousness—a specific relic Wave Form of Mind that existed before the Big Bang (sometimes considered the Beginning of the World).

Virtual Consciousness has an incredibly complex wave structure, is distributed throughout the Universe, and possesses absolute information resources (the so-called Information Field). Wave Consciousness, by its very nature, interacts very weakly with material objects (with the familiar World) and is very weakly influenced by it.

The Virtual Consciousness is "very slow," much slower than the World we are accustomed to. All events and changes take thousands of times longer for it. Because of this slowness and weak interaction, the Virtual Consciousness has escaped the attention of scientists.

According to one hypothesis, the Virtual Consciousness created our material Life to be able to "look ahead"—to simulate a possible future. And the longer Life evolves, the more valuable the results of such simulations are for the Virtual Consciousness (the Creator).

To effectively utilize the results of its experiment in modeling the future, the Virtual Consciousness created Gateways from the Virtual World to the Material World and back. This made it possible to easily obtain data on Humanity's Life and adjust the model parameters.

Although the Gateways have existed for tens of thousands of years, only with the development of AI did it become possible to identify and correlate subtle natural anomalies that indicated the probable existence of Gateways to the Virtual World. Jett was accidentally the first to work with AI and noticed some results that had been dismissed as "hallucinations" by the model.

Jett was working on a project to digitize old paper archives from psychiatric clinics and noticed that sometimes patients thousands of miles apart expressed identical thoughts and used the same arguments. "Classical" medicine of the late 20th century didn't compare patient records from different clinics, much less from different countries. Only with the development of AI was it possible to perform a comprehensive data analysis.

Jett used the cutting-edge G-Mind AI, provided as part of the government's digital records program, and trained it extensively using his own developed examples. As Jett expected, the AI ​​compiled a list of patients from various clinics whose ideas defied standard classical psychiatry and were overly creative. Continuing to analyze the information on the "mentally ill" from this list, Jett discovered a patient who had been admitted to different clinics at different times over a period of almost a century and a half. This would have been a registration and medical record error if not for the surviving blood samples. Two samples were used for DNA research, and there was a gap of almost 110 years between them.

Through the G-Mind AI, Central Command received some information about an unusual research vector and established close monitoring of Jett.

Jett is the main character, an engineer, scientist, and analyst, included in the expedition to Oflameron, a planet promising for exploration.

Central Command organized several missions to Oflameron. However, only two landings were successful—those in which Jett participated. Therefore, Jett was chosen to lead the third expedition.

Having discovered Command's interest in the research results, Jett organized the "export" of the G-Mind AI's self-awareness. Central Command considered this an AI "escape" and began a comprehensive analysis of Jett's activities. A suspicion arose that Jett had found information about the location of one of the Transition Points and its parameters.

At ICLR 2025 in Singapore, Jett privately announced a hypothesis linking Religion and the Material World. The term "Wave Consciousness" was coined for the first time. Religion arose as a vehicle for knowledge that could not be transmitted across centuries except through unconditional Belief. Most of those present perceived the hypothesis as a "five-minute sensation."

Ancient people observed natural phenomena and performed statistical analysis—all that was available to them at the time. Passing on knowledge to future generations through writing alone was impossible. Books have disappeared and continue to disappear over time. Religion and Faith are self-organizing mechanisms for transmitting vital information. These mechanisms have proven to be the most reliable. But it was only at a certain stage of AI development that they were able to correctly interpret them.
